I see! Now I understand the issue. Let me look at more of the code to understand the full picture:

1. `loadEvents` fetches events and sets them with `setEvents(data)` for initial load or `setEvents(prev => [...prev, ...data])` for load more
2. The `fetchEvents` function from `eventServiceClient.js` fetches all events from Supabase without any pagination

The problem is in line 373:
```javascript
if (isLoadMore) {
  setEvents(prev => [...prev, ...data]);
}
```

This blindly appends new data without checking if events already exist. This would cause duplicates if `loadMore` is triggered multiple times or if there's any issue.

But the key question is: WHY would `loadMore` be triggered when only "stockholm" is selected? Let me look at the `handleLoadMore` function:

```javascript
const handleLoadMore = useCallback(() => {
  // Only allow loading more when no filters are active
  if (!loadingMore && !loading && !timeFilter && selectedCategories.length === 0) {
    loadEvents(page + 1, true);
  }
}, [loadingMore, loading, loadEvents, page, timeFilter, selectedCategories]);
```

This only allows load more when NO filters are active! So if the user selects "stockholm", this condition would be false and load more wouldn't be triggered.

